<title>KUWAIT: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>KUWAIT GOVERNMENT LIST (961016)</p>
<p> **************************************************************</p>
<p> * 15 Oct 96 -  Sheikh Jaber accepted the nomination of a new *</p>
<p> *		  cabinet by Crown Prince and Prime Minister    *</p>
<p> *		  Sheikh Saad. The new cabinet included four    *</p>
<p> *		  elected deputies.				     *</p>
<p> **************************************************************</p>
<p> Emir (Head of State)............SHEIKH JABER al-Ahmad al-Sabah</p>
<p>Heir Apparent (Crown Prince)</p>
<p>    &amp; Prime Minister............SHEIKH SAAD al-Abdulla al-Sabah</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>CABINET (Formed 15 October 1996)</p>
<p> Prime Minister...............................See Heir Apparent</p>
<p>First Deputy Prime Minister &amp; Foreign</p>
<p>    Minister.....................SHEIKH SABAH al-Ahmad al-Sabah</p>
<p>Deputy Prime Minister &amp; Defence</p>
<p>    Minister...............SHEIKH SALEM Sabah al-Salem al-Sabah</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister &amp; Finance Minister......Nasser al-RODHAN</p>
<p>			     - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Communications, Electricity &amp; Water..............Jassem al-OUN</p>
<p> Defence..........................................See Deputy PM</p>
<p> Education &amp; Higher Education................Abdulla al-GHUNAIM</p>
<p> Finance..........................................See Deputy PM</p>
<p> Foreign....................................See First Deputy PM</p>
<p>Information, Public</p>
<p>    Health (acting).................SHEIKH SAUD Nasser al-Sabah</p>
<p> Interior.......................SHEIKH MOHAMMAD Khaled al-Sabah</p>
<p>Justice, Endowments &amp; Islamic</p>
<p>    Affairs (elected MP)........................Mohammad SHARAR</p>
<p> Oil.............................................Isa al-MAZEEDI</p>
<p> Planning.........................................Ali al-ZMEI'A</p>
<p> Public Works (elected MP).....................Abdulla al-HAJRI</p>
<p> Social Affairs &amp; Labour (elected MP)...........Ahmad al-KULAIB</p>
<p> Trade &amp; Industry (elected MP)..................Jassem al-MUDAF</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS OF STATE:</p>
<p> Adminstrative Development Affairs........See Planning Minister</p>
<p> Cabinet Affairs...........................Abdul-Aziz al-DAKHIL</p>
<p> Housing Affairs......................See Public Works Minister</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor.........Sheikh SALEM Abdul-Aziz al-Sabah</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>Parliament Speaker....To be elected after new parliament holds</p>
<p>first session October 20</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542-</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			   (End government list)</p>
</text>
